# Display Manager & DE Base
# sddm is the display manager; xorg-server is its hard dependency and
# is therefore in this list too. Earlier code moved both OUT of the
# pacstrap transaction to work around an xorg-server-common / xorg-server
# dir-vs-file conflict, but the zzzz98-xorg-server-fix.hook now handles
# that during the pacstrap transaction (see airootfs/etc/pacman.d/hooks/).
# The post-pacstrap `pacman -Sy` step was failing with "not enough free
# disk space" because the chroot's /var/cache is tiny; removing the
# redundant post-pacstrap install is cleaner anyway.
sddm
xorg-server
xorg-xwayland
wayland
xorg-xinit
# The 'breeze' SDDM theme ships as part of the plasma-desktop package
# (already in this list), not as a separate sddm-breeze package. Earlier
# build attempts added a non-existent 'sddm-breeze' which made pacstrap
# fail with 'target not found: sddm-breeze'. No action needed here.

# Hardware / Drivers
mesa
vulkan-intel
vulkan-radeon
xf86-video-amdgpu
xf86-video-nouveau
xf86-video-intel
# Touch/touchpad/mouse input for the X11 session. kwin-x11 above means X11
# is an offered login session, not just Wayland -- and unlike Wayland
# (where KWin talks to libinput directly), X11 needs this driver or input
# doesn't work at all there: no mouse, no keyboard, no touch. It's an
# *optional* dependency of xorg-server, so pacman never pulls it in on its
# own. libinput itself is listed explicitly too rather than relying on it
# being pulled in transitively by Plasma.
xf86-input-libinput
libinput
# Accelerometer/orientation, for auto-rotate on a convertible touchscreen.
iio-sensor-proxy
alsa-utils
alsa-firmware
sof-firmware
pipewire
wireplumber
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack

